A||||3||Blaster||Need some help here..||||8||
Z||000000||Blaster||03-04-2001||12:40 AM||||Ok, I had to drop my cradle to fix my exhaust once again. Anyways, exhaust isn't the problem right now. I have dropped my cradle pretty much the same way everytime, except of learning new things and being more careful. I haven't had this problem before, just this time. My tires seem to be pointing outward. Not LEANING, but actually facing out. Can't go over 5 mphs and starts sliding everywhere. I am confused because I was very careful with supporting A arms and the hubs. I really need to figure this out cuz I need to get it rolling, in a straight line <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> , again. Thanks.||||reg||8
Z||000001||Fiero_Freak||03-04-2001||09:48 AM||||Did you leave your struts in when you removed the cradle?  You may need to loosen your strut to spindle nuts and push in hard while you tighten them.  You can also adjust the toe with the toe link that attaches to the back of that same spindle.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||TheFiero64||03-04-2001||10:11 AM||||I agree with Fiero_Freak. I think your struts are adjusted wrong. loosen the 2 bottom strut bolts and press in on the strut and tighten them up.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||03-04-2001||02:41 PM||||If you disconnected the struts at the knuckle (two large 24mm bolts) you will need to have the wheels re-aligned..........if you took the struts loose from the top (three 13mm bolts) you should notice that one of these bolts on the top of the strut plate is slightly longer than the others. This is the bolt (stud) that goes toward the inside of the engine bay. It is possible to twist that strut and spring assembly enough to give the condition you are describing.<P>What I would do is make sure that the strut is installed properly on the top of the strut tower, make sure that the two 24mm's are tightened and then take it down and have it aligned......||||reg||1
